# Windows Authentication Methods

## Lab Overview
This lab explores the (2) Authentication methods used by Windows for users to access domain-provided services

## Objectives
- Understand the how Kerberos and NTLM authenticate users
- Identify the components of Kerberos that allow authentication
- Learn how NTLM can be used securely for compatible systems

## Key Concepts
| Kerberos | Windows authentication protcol for logging into directory services |
| NTLM (NT LAN Manager| Legacy authentication protocol kept for compatibility purposes |
| KDC(Key Distribution Center) | Kerberos authentication service that runs on a DC |
| TGT(Ticket Granting Ticket) | Temporary means of authentication presented to a KDC to validate a user and request TGS |
| Session Key | Temporary key provided along with TGT to gain access to a specific service |
| TGS(Ticket Granting Service) | Function of the KDC that provides TGS tickets to users to gain access to services on the network |
| SPN(Service Principal Name) | Unique identifier providing which account a service belongs to and the encryption method | 
| Service Owner Hash | Long-term key used to encrypt part of a session key ensuring on the service can decrypt/read client identity information |

